  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Local Response to TB in the Kyrgyz Republic, TB LON</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kyrgyz Republic):  To accelerate the elimination of TB in the Kyrgyz Republic, USAID partners with local non-government organizations to enable local solutions and sustainability of the TB response. The TB Local Organizations Network (LON) activity supports prevention, care, and treatment of TB through a direct agreement with local organizations, which is a key component of the USAID TB Portfolio&apos;s localization efforts. TB LON partners exclusively with local organizations and implements locally-generated solutions to improve TB services. In close collaboration with the Cure TB activity, the TB LON activity contributes to reducing the burden of DR-TB in the Kyrgyz Republic. To achieve this, the activity will continue to increase active TB case detection among contacts of TB patients through community-based detection; contribute to the increase of the treatment success rate among TB defaulters through case management; improve the enabling environment for reduced stigma and discrimination of the TB patients through raising awareness among the general population; and ensure advocacy for strengthening the country&apos;s national dialogue for TB services, improved data for decision making, updated policies, and reduced stigma and discrimination...This activity  also supports ICS Mission Objective 3.2: Government Institutions that can effectively formulate and implement policies and provide quality services in an equitable, transparent, and accountable way.  It also supports CDCS DO 2: Robust and Diversified Economic Opportunities for the People of the Kyrgyz Republic, IR 2.2: Improved equitable access to quality health services. Specifically, this activity will contribute to sub-IR 2.2.3: Case detection and treatment adherence to control infection disease threats, especially HIV and TB, improved...This IM contributes $935,000 toward the $6,000,000 FY 2022 Operating Unit TB directive. .. .</narrative>
  </description>
